  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-04-20T02:51:01.680Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "It would be a great feature, especially because all the blush effects on the avatars just looks bad without the transparency (who don't enable the shaders on the avatars), so at least, we could just disable the blush effect by this parameter if the shaders are turned off. Also, even if we try to use the Poiyomi's shader and set the fallback shader to transparent, it does absolutely nothing.\n\nAlso it could provide more performance benefits too, since it would allow the avatar creators to both utilize the UV tile discard and the usage of blendshape driven toggles too, so the creators could make both animation clips for hiding the object by the UV discard system or by a blendshape if the player turned off the shaders on the avatars.",
